    pr_ref:  # ef1f
    description: "A Swift subscript with no external label is named after its internal parameter name: `subscript(i: Int)` becomes `subscript(i:)`, so renaming `i`, which callers never write, moves its stable id. A subscript's external label (`subscript(key k: K)`) is identity; the internal name is not.\n\nThe fix moves every unlabelled subscript's id, so it needs a scheme bump. It was left out of PR 5 (v17) deliberately.\n\nFound by PR 5 agent 1 (WI-lonoh). Repro: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr5/lonoh/residual_fixtures/R.swift."  # ef1f
    fields: {}  # ef1f
